[*] GTKWave save file for gtkwave_example.vcd
[*] This file pre-loads signals so they're visible immediately
[*]
[*] To regenerate: Open VCD in GTKWave, arrange signals, then File -> Write Save File
[*]
[*] Signal format: [hierarchy] [signal_name] [color] [format]
[*] Hierarchy levels: 0=top, 1=first level, etc.
[*]
[*] Note: This is a template. GTKWave will auto-populate when you:
[*] 1. Open gtkwave_example.vcd
[*] 2. Expand hierarchy (SST panel on left)
[*] 3. Select signals: clk, a, b, y, enable, counter
[*] 4. Drag to waveform viewer (right panel)
[*] 5. Save: File -> Write Save File
[*]
[*] After saving, this file will contain the actual signal configuration
[*] Then you can use: gtkwave gtkwave_example.vcd gtkwave_example.gtkw
